249 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/E (A total of 26 participants took part in a series of workshop pilots focused on developing team-skills through the implementation of sustainable crafts, the following data presented is part of a methodology developed by the international project TB-GOBRA. The multi-background and multi-cultural participants volunteered to take part in the impact study, where they were asked to take proficiency tests prior and following the workshop pilots. 20 of them answered the test after the experience.)
/Pg 10 0 R
/K [3]
>>
endobj
250 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/E (In addition, the participants studying at the University of Lapland were asked to reflect on their experience, we received 17 essays. The participants who answered the questionnaire and wrote the essays were partly the same and different. In addition, observations of the activities from the facilitators and documentation of the craft processes and results are used as research data.)
/Pg 10 0 R
/K [4]
>>
endobj
251 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/E (The feedback highlights the participants' positive experiences with the workshops, emphasising the friendly, inclusive, and supportive atmosphere fostered by professional and approachable facilitators. Many found the activities enjoyable, insightful, and engaging, offering opportunities to learn about sustainable crafting, traditional Finnish techniques, and collaborative practices. The workshops helped participants socialise, break the ice, and discover shared interests, enhancing their sense of community.)
/Pg 10 0 R
/K [5]
>>
endobj
252 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/E (However, a recurring suggestion was the need for more explicit workshop descriptions, objectives, and information on post-workshop requirements to help participants make more informed choices. Some participants noted that improved clarity in instructions during the workshops would also enhance the experience. Overall, the workshops were described as valuable, inspiring, and worthwhile, with many expressing interest in more frequent opportunities for similar activities. Several participants discovered new hobbies and appreciated the use of natural and sustainable materials, which were seen as both beautiful and environmentally friendly.)
/Pg 10 0 R
/K [6]
>>
endobj
