<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/E (The Agri-food production workshop was quite short and very simple. There were only four of us and the leader, and we played a quiz on the Kahoot platform related to agricultural food production. In addition, at the beginning we discussed why "team-building" is an important tool. Although the topics raised in Kahoot sparked discussion among the participants, I think Kahoot was perhaps not the best possible implementation. I did learn something new with the help of the quiz, but otherwise the workshop was quite short and poor in content. All the participants were again really nice and we had a good time, which was perhaps the strength of this workshop.)
/Pg 19 0 R
/K [3]
>>
endobj
343 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/E (Since the workshop ended so early, we went to see the "bike felting" workshop. Based on the name, I had absolutely no idea what the workshop would contain. It was interesting to see and learn how raw wool is worked, and its "felting" using a wheel. Unfortunately, the developed method did not fully work, but with the help of failures, we thought together as a group on how to improve the method and solve the problems that came up. Working together was fun, even if the execution was perhaps not exactly what was planned. It was nice to notice how the participants were eager to participate in each work step, and without the group, the wool sheet would not have been completed.)
/Pg 19 0 R
/K [4]
>>
