406 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/E (This workshop, I would say, was my favorite of all the ones I took part in. Before this activity, I had zero knowledge of how wool is processed and used. I had never seen wool directly from a farm nor touched it. For me, this whole process was about learning and getting hands on it. I was excited to take part in every single part of the process. At the same time, it was fun and I got to work together with many other participants. I remember the moment when we all finally attached the blanket to the bike and as soon as the guy on the bike began rolling it, we could feel the unity of the whole group happily showing their emotion by clapping or screaming. Also, the way everyone tried to find a solution when the rope broke the first time and how we all together tried to make it work and succeeded in the end was something special. I would really enjoy having more chances to be part of a group like that.)
/Pg 27 0 R
/K [2]
>>
