/S /P
/E (In this session, we were paired off and started by introducing ourselves, discussing our backgrounds, and explaining what brought us to the workshop, how much experience we have with embroidery. This was a great way to break the ice, setting a warm, collaborative tone for the activity. Each of us embroidered a design on a small black fabric piece inspired by a topic we wanted to discuss. For me, it was mental health, how one can reach out for help and what kind of barriers he/she must overcome. My partner had the theme of identity a reflection on her journey as an immigrant looking for a sense of belonging and new roots. Both of our pieces had roots, engagement, healthy connections as common topics.)
/Pg 37 0 R
/K [3]
