519 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/E (knowing what to expect going in, the activity turned out to be a lot different that I had anticipated. However I really enjoyed learning about the topic, and was fascinated with both the traditional and modern takes on the craft. I learnt that blanket embroidery was traditionally done with wool that was made and dyed by hand, then used in winter to embroider the actual wool blankets. This definitely inspired me to want to have a go at hand dying yarn or fabric when I get back home because it sounds like a lot of fun, and I would love the experimentation side of it. I was also really interested to learn that women in a family would work on embroidering a blanket for a new bride to take with her, particularly as in my culture there are similar traditions, and as an engaged person I found it fascinating. I definitely plan to have another go at embroidering a blanket in the future. As far as the workshop itself, I really enjoyed doing the embroidery, but as someone who already had experience in embroidery, I think it was a lot more difficult for those who had never picked up a needle before. It would have been nice if there had been some instructions on how to do specific stitches.)
/Pg 38 0 R
/K [8]
>>
