<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/E (Felting was very relaxing, and we shared a compact space and tools as a group. I had fallen before, so it was nice to help my neighbors. It was great to use raw wool again as well as naturally dyed wool. The smell of wool was very intoxicating. They say time flies when you're comfortable, and that was the case with this one. The felting and scratching could have continued indefinitely.)
/Pg 44 0 R
/K [10]
>>
endobj
578 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/E (All in all, during the last few days, I have noticed that, for example, crafts are a really good way to cultivate group spirit and do things together. I hadn't done handicrafts in a long time, especially with soft materials, so the workshops were relaxing and at the same time I noticed that I also learned something new. It must be said that practicing handicrafts under natural conditions or with the most durable materials is not that complicated. How could even these fairly simple workshops be implemented using the most durable materials? So we have years of heritage from organic methods, so it was nice how they were utilized in this course/workshop as a whole. Organizing more sustainable workshops is therefore not impossible, and hopefully we will see more of them in the future. We hope that similar projects will be funded in the future.)
/Pg 44 0 R
/K [11]
>>
endobj
